Define  $X$  as the midpoint of the crease of the fold  $\overline{BC}$  and  $A$  as the point of overlap that lies on both edges of the strip. Let  $\angle CXY=\theta$  where  $0^\circ<\theta<90^\circ.$  Note that  $\triangle ABX\cong\triangle ACX\sim\triangle CXY,$  and
\begin{align*}CY &= XY\tan\theta=1.5\tan\theta, 
AY &= XY\tan\left(90^\circ-\theta\right)=1.5\cot\theta, 
[ABC] &= 2\cdot[AXC] = 2\cdot\frac{XY\cdot AC}{2} = XY\cdot AC = XY\cdot\left(AY+CY\right) 
&= 1.5\left(1.5\tan\theta+1.5\cot\theta\right) = 2.25\left(\tan\theta+\frac{1}{\tan\theta}\right)
&\geq 2.25\cdot2=\boxed{4.5\text{ cm}^2}\end{align*}
from AM-GM. Equality is attained at  $\theta=45^\circ.$

